WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.650
If the Sun disappeared right now,

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:03.840
you wouldn't even notice
for another 8 minutes!

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:06.720
That's because sunlight
doesn't reach Earth instantly.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.310
It takes approximately 8 minutes and 20
seconds to travel from the Sun to us.

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.890
So even if the Sun
vanished this very second,

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.630
we'd still see it shining in the sky.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.430
But here's something even crazier.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:21.380
Gravity also travels at the speed of light
according to Einstein's theory of general

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:22.150
relativity.

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:25.250
That means Earth wouldn't immediately
notice the Sun's disappearance

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.700
gravitationally either.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:29.330
After those 8 minutes,
sunlight would disappear.

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:34.200
The sky would become dark, and Earth would
no longer orbit the Sun in its usual path.

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:37.880
Our planet would continue moving along
its existing direction through space.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.490
Without sunlight,
temperatures would begin dropping,

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:45.130
photosynthesis would stop, and life as we
know it would face a catastrophic crisis.

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:48.190
All because of something that
happened 8 minutes earlier.

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:49.960
Would you survive the first day?

